# Volta Pension Trust — Governance & Continuity Review

*The board has called a cyber-governance and business-continuity review before its
next quarterly meeting. You are briefing it. Work this pack into recovery
priorities and a clear-eyed list of the governance gaps — then write the executive
memo and the recovery-priority table.*

---

## 1. The institution

Volta Pension Trust manages retirement savings for about **__MEMBERS__ members**
and pays monthly benefits to **__PENSIONERS__ pensioners** who depend on that
money to live. Core services:

- **Benefits Payment System** — pays pensioners each month (the crown jewel of
  *availability*).
- **Contributions Portal** — employers and members pay in.
- **Member Records Database** — personal and financial data.
- **Public Website** — information only, no transactions.

**Governance posture:** the board meets quarterly but has **no standing cyber
agenda item** and **no named accountable executive** (no CISO or DPO). The IT
policy was last approved **__POLICY_AGE__ years ago**. There is **no tested
disaster-recovery plan** and **no crisis-command structure**.

## 2. Business impact analysis (BIA)

| Service | Board-mandated RTO | Current RTO | Board RPO | Current RPO | Impact of an outage |
|---------|--------------------|-------------|-----------|-------------|---------------------|
| **Benefits Payment System** | **__BP_RTO_REQUIRED__ h** | **__BP_RTO_CURRENT__ h** | 1 h | __BP_RPO_CURRENT__ h | **GHS __IMPACT_PER_DAY__ / day** + pensioner hardship, reputational damage |
| Contributions Portal | 12 h | 36 h | 4 h | 24 h | Delayed contributions; member frustration |
| Member Records DB | 8 h | 24 h | 2 h | 24 h | Service degradation; data-loss exposure |
| Public Website | 72 h | 48 h | 24 h | 24 h | Minor — informational only |

Backups run weekly to a networked drive and have **never been restore-tested**.

## 3. The current board pack (for your critique)

The security slide the board currently receives reports:

- "**Attacks blocked this quarter: 4.2 million**" (the headline metric)
- "Firewall uptime: 99.98%"
- "Antivirus installed on 100% of laptops"

It does **not** report detection/response times, patch compliance, MFA adoption,
or whether backups have ever been restored. A document titled **"Password
Policy"** turns out to be a **step-by-step MFA-enrolment walkthrough**.

## 4. The regulatory frame

As a financial institution, the Trust is likely **Critical Information
Infrastructure** under the **Cybersecurity Act 2020 (Act 1038)**, with incident-
reporting duties to the **CSA / CERT-GH**, and it holds personal data under the
**Data Protection Act 2012 (Act 843)** (DPC).

